Catch broadlyCatch a specific statusLet it propagate Python<pre><code>from pokelance.exceptions import PokeLanceException

try:
    pokemon = await client.pokemon.fetch_pokemon(user_input)
except PokeLanceException as exc:
    await ctx.send(f"Something went wrong: {exc}")
</code></pre> Python<pre><code>from pokelance.exceptions import ResourceNotFound

try:
    pokemon = await client.pokemon.fetch_pokemon(user_input)
except ResourceNotFound as exc:
    suggestions = ", ".join(exc.suggestions or [])
    await ctx.send(f"Couldn't find '{user_input}'. Did you mean: {suggestions}?")
</code></pre> <p>In a FastAPI handler, for instance, you may want an unhandled <code>ResourceNotFound</code> to naturally become a 404, see the FastAPI recipe for a complete example with an exception handler registered at the app level.</p>
